  "goodToKnow": "Verwunden means to wound, especially in war or by weapons: schwer verwundet (seriously wounded), and figuratively, to hurt emotionally. For accidents, Germans say verletzen. Der/die Verwundete is a wounded person. Verwundbar means vulnerable, and die Achillesferse is everyone's weak spot. Don't confuse it with verwundern (to astonish): Es verwundert mich nicht. From die Wunde (wound)."
